Pf3D7_01_v3	chado	pseudogenic_transcript	560474	561534	.	-	.	ID=PF3D7_0114600.1;comment=stevor (subtelomeric%2C variable open reading frames) genes were originally identified as multicopy markers for fingerprinting parasites. With approximately 30 copies per haploid genome%2C they encode the STEVOR proteins%2C which are clonally variant%2C expressed on both merozoites and at the surface of infected erythrocytes. STEVOR is expressed much more prevalently in patient isolates than in laboratory isolates. Similar to (but clearly distinct from) RIFINs%2C surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion.;literature=PMID:18474651,PMID:14747138,PMID:1706114,PMID:19229319;Parent=PF3D7_0114600;Dbxref=MPMP:PF3D7_0114600;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 209-220%3B,%3Bquery 292-312%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-313%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-185%3B,%3Bquery 244-268%3B;orthologous_to=,,PfalciparumIT:PFIT_0113400 link%3DPFIT_0113400.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Dstevor%2C pseudogene%3B match_name%3Dorthomcl:orthomcl: PFIT_0113400.1:pep -> PF3D7_0114600.1:pep%3B rank%3D0;polypeptide_domain=pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF02009.12%3B%3BE()%3D2.0E-15%3Bscore%3D57.4%3Bquery 29-210%3Bdescription%3DRifin_STEVOR,pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF02009.12%3B%3BE()%3D5.4E-14%3Bscore%3D52.6%3Bquery 268-308%3Bdescription%3DRifin_STEVOR,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006374 :%09Variant surface antigen Stevor%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BTIGR_TIGRFAMS:TIGR01478%3B%3Bscore%3D1.3E-116%3Bquery 1-308%3Bdescription%3DVariant surface antigen Stevor,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006374 :%09Variant surface antigen Stevor%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BPfam:PF17410%3B%3Bscore%3D5.6E-116%3Bquery 31-308%3Bdescription%3DVariant surface antigen Stevor;product=term%3Dstevor%2C pseudogene%3B,rank%3D1%3Bterm%3DPIR protein%2C pseudogene%3B;signal_peptide=signalp%3B%3Bquery 1-22%3Bcleavage_site_probability%3D0.151;transmembrane_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 186-208%3B,%3Bquery 221-243%3B,%3Bquery 269-