Pf3D7_02_v3	chado	mRNA	127203	129089	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_0202500.1;comment=Early transcribed membrane protein (ETRAMP) family member.  Plasmodium conserved family with greater than ten members in P. falciparum.  ETRAMPs are abundantly expressed early in the intraerythrocytic cycle and are small (frequently less than 200 aa) integral membrane proteins that are localized within the parasitophorous vacuolar membrane (PVM).  All members have signal peptides plus a transmembrane domain.  Some members are expressed during hepatocyte development and their targeted gene disruption results in a block in hepatocyte development. absolute transcriptional activity peaks in late schizonts by nuclear run-on hybridization (PMID:19151330);literature=PMID:15699336,PMID:16420351,PMID:12686607,PMID:12615320;Parent=PF3D7_0202500;Dbxref=UniProtKB:O96128,MPMP:PF3D7_0202500,OPI:PFB0120w;Ontology_term=GO:0020005,GO:1903561,GO:0005634;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-49%3B;eupathdb_uc=21293;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-107%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 73-106%3B;orthologous_to=Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1102800 link%3DPF3D7_1102800.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pmalariae:PmUG01_04029900 link%3DPmUG01_04029900.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Povale:PocGH01_04027300 link%3DPocGH01_04027300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_1101300 link%3DPRCDC_1101300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0201600 link%3DPRCDC_0201600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C PvivaxP01:PVP01_0422600 link%3DPVP01_0422600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pknowlesi:PKNH_0418600 link%3DPKNH_0418600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B cluster_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL4878%3B program%3DOrthoMCL%3B rank%3D0,;polypeptide_domain=pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF09716.6%3B%3BE()%3D1.3E-17%3Bscore%3D63.5%3Bquery 1-75%3Bdescription%3DETRAMP,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006389 :%09Early transcribed membrane protein (ETRAMP)%3BTIGR_TIGRFAMS:TIGR01495%3B%3Bscore%3D9.1E-32%3Bquery 1-81%3Bdescription%3DEarly transcribe