Pf3D7_02_v3	chado	mRNA	860466	861504	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_0221400.1;comment=stevor (subtelomeric%2C variable open reading frames) genes were originally identified as multicopy markers for fingerprinting parasites. With approximately 30 copies per haploid genome%2C they encode the STEVOR proteins%2C which are clonally variant%2C expressed on both merozoites and at the surface of infected erythrocytes. STEVOR is expressed much more prevalently in patient isolates than in laboratory isolates. Similar to (but clearly distinct from) RIFINs%2C surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion.;literature=PMID:14747138,PMID:1706114,PMID:25011110,PMID:18474651,PMID:19229319;Parent=PF3D7_0221400;Dbxref=UniProtKB:O96283,MPMP:PF3D7_0221400;Ontology_term=GO:0016020,GO:0020036,GO:0020013;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 27-229%3B,%3Bquery 290-307%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-308%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-3%3B,%3Bquery 253-266%3B;orthologous_to=Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1040200 link%3DPF3D7_1040200.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1040200.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,PfalciparumIT:PFIT_0500700 link%3DPFIT_0500700.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Dstevor%3B match_name%3Dorthomcl:orthomcl: PFIT_0500700.1:pep -> PF3D7_0221400.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1479500 link%3DPF3D7_1479500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1479500.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1254600 link%3DPF3D7_1254600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1254600.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1100700 link%3DPF3D7_1100700.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%2C pseudogene%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1100700.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1254300 link%3DPF3D7_1254300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1254300.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0832000 link%3DPF3D7_0832000.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1372500 l