Pf3D7_04_v3	chado	mRNA	42032	43374	.	-	.	ID=PF3D7_0400300.1;comment=rif (repetitive interspersed family) genes were originally identified by Weber%3B they encode clonally variant RIFIN proteins%2C which are likely expressed on the infected erythrocyte surface%2C in Maurer's clefts and on merozoites. Originally classed with stevors%2C rifs are clearly a distinct family%2C with 150 or so copies per haploid genome. Surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion. A-type rifin (PMID:18197962);literature=PMID:10430943,PMID:17719658,PMID:10562315,PMID:25751816,PMID:2842673;Parent=PF3D7_0400300;Dbxref=MPMP:PF3D7_0400300,UniProtKB:Q8I219;Ontology_term=GO:0020033,GO:0020002,GO:0020035,GO:0020013,GO:0020036,GO:0020003;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 351-370%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-371%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-327%3B;orthologous_to=Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0222500 link%3DPF3D7_0222500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Drifin%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0222500.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1479700 link%3DPF3D7_1479700.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3DPIR protein%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1479700.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0101900 link%3DPF3D7_0101900.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3DPIR protein%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0101900.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Preichenowi:PRCDC_0049600 link%3DPRCDC_0049600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Drifin%3B match_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL6111%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0101000 link%3DPF3D7_0101000.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Drifin%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0101000.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1000200 link%3DPF3D7_1000200.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Drifin%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1000200.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0732900 link%3DPF3D7_0732900.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Drifin%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0732900.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1480000 link%3DPF3D7_1480000.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3DPIR protein%3Bmatch_