Pf3D7_04_v3	chado	mRNA	66601	67573	.	-	.	ID=PF3D7_0400800.1;comment=stevor (subtelomeric%2C variable open reading frames) genes were originally identified as multicopy markers for fingerprinting parasites. With approximately 30 copies per haploid genome%2C they encode the STEVOR proteins%2C which are clonally variant%2C expressed on both merozoites and at the surface of infected erythrocytes. STEVOR is expressed much more prevalently in patient isolates than in laboratory isolates. Similar to (but clearly distinct from) RIFINs%2C surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion.;literature=PMID:14747138,PMID:25011110,PMID:1706114,PMID:18474651,PMID:19229319;Parent=PF3D7_0400800;Dbxref=MPMP:PF3D7_0400800,UniProtKB:Q8I215;Ontology_term=GO:0016020,GO:0020036,GO:0020013;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-174%3B,%3Bquery 273-289%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-290%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 198-249%3B;orthologous_to=PfalciparumIT:PFIT_bin03100 link%3DPFIT_bin03100.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Dstevor%3B match_name%3Dorthomcl:orthomcl: PFIT_bin03100.1:pep -> PF3D7_0400800.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0201300 link%3DPF3D7_0201300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0201300.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0101800 link%3DPF3D7_0101800.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0101800.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1100700 link%3DPF3D7_1100700.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%2C pseudogene%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1100700.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Preichenowi:PRCDC_0033800 link%3DPRCDC_0033800.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Dstevor%3B match_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL6110%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0732000 link%3DPF3D7_0732000.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0732000.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0901600 link%3DPF3D7_0901600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_