Pf3D7_04_v3	chado	pseudogenic_transcript	89153	90184	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_0401500.1;comment=stevor (subtelomeric%2C variable open reading frames) genes were originally identified as multicopy markers for fingerprinting parasites. With approximately 30 copies per haploid genome%2C they encode the STEVOR proteins%2C which are clonally variant%2C expressed on both merozoites and at the surface of infected erythrocytes. STEVOR is expressed much more prevalently in patient isolates than in laboratory isolates. Similar to (but clearly distinct from) RIFINs%2C surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion.;literature=PMID:1706114,PMID:19229319,PMID:14747138,PMID:18474651;Parent=PF3D7_0401500;Dbxref=MPMP:PF3D7_0401500;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-181%3B,%3Bquery 293-309%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-311%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 205-269%3B;orthologous_to=Preichenowi:PRCDC_0013700 link%3DPRCDC_0013700.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Dstevor%3B match_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL6109%3B rank%3D0,PfalciparumIT:PFIT_1401700 link%3DPFIT_1401700.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Dstevor%3B match_name%3Dorthomcl:orthomcl: PFIT_1401700.1:pep -> PF3D7_0401500.1:pep%3B rank%3D0;product=term%3Dstevor%2C pseudogene%3B,rank%3D1%3Bterm%3DPIR protein%2C pseudogene%3B;signal_peptide=signalp%3B%3Bquery 1-22%3Bcleavage_site_probability%3D0.242;transmembrane_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 182-204%3B,%3Bquery 270-292%3B;translation=mntyyvklllftflinilvlphnenyinnhyniiliqnntqrttiksrllaqtqnhnphyhndpelkemidklneeaikkyqqthepyeqlkelveksetkltggndaepmstlekelleiyeemfghkndimlkscmyqnddeksdksssc#ctdtnnaklattkgkdkylkhlkhrctrgicscsvgsvfitligllvakaaavdafkivtasiatcskcassitisnmfnnasivaalqkcgvlvatngvsdgvgtavgtattafnpygiaalvlilvavaliilyiwlyrrrknswkheckkhlck
