Pf3D7_04_v3	chado	mRNA	92418	94121	.	-	.	ID=PF3D7_0401600.1;comment=rif (repetitive interspersed family) genes were originally identified by Weber%3B they encode clonally variant RIFIN proteins%2C which are likely expressed on the infected erythrocyte surface%2C in Maurer's clefts and on merozoites. Originally classed with stevors%2C rifs are clearly a distinct family%2C with 150 or so copies per haploid genome. Surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion. RIFIN undefined type%3B based on HMM-search%2C A. Claessens (U of Edinburgh%2C unpublished data 2007);literature=PMID:17719658,PMID:2842673,PMID:10430943,PMID:10562315;Parent=PF3D7_0401600;Dbxref=MPMP:PF3D7_0401600;Ontology_term=GO:0016020,GO:0020036;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 25-253%3B,%3Bquery 328-347%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-348%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-4%3B,%3Bquery 277-304%3B;orthologous_to=PfalciparumIT:PFIT_0400300 link%3DPFIT_0400300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Drifin%3B match_name%3Dorthomcl:orthomcl: PFIT_0400300.1:pep -> PF3D7_0401600.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Preichenowi:PRCDC_0004700 link%3DPRCDC_0004700.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0401600 link%3DPF3D7_0401600.2:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B cluster_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL5419%3B program%3DOrthoMCL%3B rank%3D0,;polypeptide_domain=pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF02009.12%3B%3BE()%3D6.1E-66%3Bscore%3D223.3%3Bquery 28-346%3Bdescription%3DRifin_STEVOR,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006373 :%09Variant surface antigen Rifin%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BPfam:PF02009%3B%3Bscore%3D2.0E-38%3Bquery 42-346%3Bdescription%3DVariant surface antigen Rifin;product=term%3Drifin%3B,rank%3D1%3Bterm%3DPIR protein%3B;signal_peptide=signalp%3B%3Bquery 1-24%3Bcleavage_site_probability%3D0.677;transmembrane_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 5-24%3B,%3Bquery 254-276%3B,%3Bquery 305-327%3B;
