Pf3D7_04_v3	chado	mRNA	967087	968273	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_0421200.1;comment=rif (repetitive interspersed family) genes were originally identified by Weber%3B they encode clonally variant RIFIN proteins%2C which are likely expressed on the infected erythrocyte surface%2C in Maurer's clefts and on merozoites. Originally classed with stevors%2C rifs are clearly a distinct family%2C with 150 or so copies per haploid genome. Surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion. B-type rifin (PMID:18197962);literature=PMID:17719658,PMID:10562315,PMID:2842673,PMID:10430943;Parent=PF3D7_0421200;Dbxref=MPMP:PF3D7_0421200,OPI:PFD1010w,UniProtKB:Q8IFQ3;Ontology_term=GO:0020002,GO:0016020,GO:0020033;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-6%3B,%3Bquery 327-346%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-347%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 27-303%3B;orthologous_to=Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0632600 link%3DPF3D7_0632600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0115300 link%3DPF3D7_0115300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0016600 link%3DPRCDC_0016600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B cluster_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL5270%3B program%3DOrthoMCL%3B rank%3D0;polypeptide_domain=pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF02009.12%3B%3BE()%3D3.7E-88%3Bscore%3D296.3%3Bquery 25-346%3Bdescription%3DRifin_STEVOR,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006373 :%09Variant surface antigen Rifin%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BPfam:PF02009%3B%3Bscore%3D1.1E-91%3Bquery 36-346%3Bdescription%3DVariant surface antigen Rifin,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006373 :%09Variant surface antigen Rifin%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BTIGR_TIGRFAMS:TIGR01477%3B%3Bscore%3D3.1E-95%3Bquery 1-346%3Bdescription%3DVariant surface antigen Rifin;product=term%3Drifin%3Bdb_xref%3DPMID:10430943%3Bevidence%3DInferred from Direct Assay,rank%3D1%3Bterm%3DPIR protein%3B;signal_peptide=signalp%3B%3Bquery 1-22%3Bcleavage_site_probability%3D0.305;transmembrane_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 7-26%3B,%3Bquery 304-326%3B;
