Pf3D7_04_v3	chado	pseudogenic_transcript	981823	982990	.	-	.	ID=PF3D7_0421500.1;comment=A-type rifin (PMID:18197962) rif (repetitive interspersed family) genes were originally identified by Weber%3B they encode clonally variant RIFIN proteins%2C which are likely expressed on the infected erythrocyte surface%2C in Maurer's clefts and on merozoites. Originally classed with stevors%2C rifs are clearly a distinct family%2C with 150 or so copies per haploid genome. Surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion.;literature=PMID:10430943,PMID:10562315,PMID:17719658,PMID:2842673;Parent=PF3D7_0421500;Dbxref=MPMP:PF3D7_0421500,OPI:PFD1020c;gPI_anchor_cleavage_site=%3Bquery 219-219%3BGPI_cleavage_site_score%3D0.516;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 316-334%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-337%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-292%3B;orthologous_to=Preichenowi:PRCDC_0011000 link%3DPRCDC_0011000.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0016200 link%3DPRCDC_0016200.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0017300 link%3DPRCDC_0017300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0023500 link%3DPRCDC_0023500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0043800 link%3DPRCDC_0043800.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0010300 link%3DPRCDC_0010300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0029400 link%3DPRCDC_0029400.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0042500 link%3DPRCDC_0042500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0028100 link%3DPRCDC_0028100.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0034500 link%3DPRCDC_0034500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0041900 link%3DPRCDC_0041900.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0028200 link%3DPRCDC_0028200.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0022600 link%3DPRCDC_0022600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0026900 link%3DPRCDC_0026900.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRC