Pf3D7_04_v3	chado	mRNA	1169521	1171286	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_0425900.1;comment=rif (repetitive interspersed family) genes were originally identified by Weber%3B they encode clonally variant RIFIN proteins%2C which are likely expressed on the infected erythrocyte surface%2C in Maurer's clefts and on merozoites. Originally classed with stevors%2C rifs are clearly a distinct family%2C with 150 or so copies per haploid genome. Surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion. A-type rifin (PMID:18197962);literature=PMID:2842673,PMID:10430943,PMID:17719658,PMID:10562315,PMID:25751816;Parent=PF3D7_0425900;Dbxref=MPMP:PF3D7_0425900,UniProtKB:Q8IFK8;Ontology_term=GO:0020033,GO:0020002,GO:0020035,GO:0020013,GO:0020036,GO:0020003;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 305-324%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-325%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-281%3B;orthologous_to=Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0223400 link%3DPF3D7_0223400.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0035300 link%3DPRCDC_0035300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B cluster_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL5422%3B program%3DOrthoMCL%3B rank%3D0;polypeptide_domain=pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF02009.12%3B%3BE()%3D7.6E-123%3Bscore%3D410.3%3Bquery 20-324%3Bdescription%3DRifin_STEVOR,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006373 :%09Variant surface antigen Rifin%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BPfam:PF02009%3B%3Bscore%3D1.5E-116%3Bquery 32-324%3Bdescription%3DVariant surface antigen Rifin,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006373 :%09Variant surface antigen Rifin%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BTIGR_TIGRFAMS:TIGR01477%3B%3Bscore%3D7.3E-135%3Bquery 1-324%3Bdescription%3DVariant surface antigen Rifin;product=term%3Drifin%3Bdb_xref%3DPMID:25751816%3Bevidence%3DInferred from Direct Assay,rank%3D1%3Bterm%3DPIR protein%3B;transmembrane_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 282-304%3B;
