Pf3D7_05_v3	chado	pseudogenic_transcript	39443	40488	.	-	.	ID=PF3D7_0500600.1;comment=stevor (subtelomeric%2C variable open reading frames) genes were originally identified as multicopy markers for fingerprinting parasites. With approximately 30 copies per haploid genome%2C they encode the STEVOR proteins%2C which are clonally variant%2C expressed on both merozoites and at the surface of infected erythrocytes. STEVOR is expressed much more prevalently in patient isolates than in laboratory isolates. Similar to (but clearly distinct from) RIFINs%2C surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion.;literature=PMID:1706114,PMID:19229319,PMID:14747138,PMID:18474651;Parent=PF3D7_0500600;Dbxref=MPMP:PF3D7_0500600;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 206-229%3B,%3Bquery 290-307%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-308%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-182%3B,%3Bquery 253-266%3B;orthologous_to=Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0221400 link%3DPF3D7_0221400.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0425500 link%3DPF3D7_0425500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1000800 link%3DPF3D7_1000800.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1372500 link%3DPF3D7_1372500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0832000 link%3DPF3D7_0832000.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0402600 link%3DPF3D7_0402600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B cluster_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL4930%3B program%3DOrthoMCL%3B rank%3D0;polypeptide_domain=pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF02009.12%3B%3BE()%3D4.2E-14%3Bscore%3D53.0%3Bquery 256-306%3Bdescription%3DRifin_STEVOR,pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF02009.12%3B%3BE()%3D7.2E-16%3Bscore%3D58.8%3Bquery 26-221%3Bdescription%3DRifin_STEVOR,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006374 :%09Variant surface antigen Stevor%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BTIGR_TIGRFAMS:TIGR01478%3B%3Bscore%3D1.1E-136%3Bquery 1-307%3Bdescription%3DVariant surface antigen Stevor,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006374 :%09Variant surface antigen Stevor%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BPfam: