Pf3D7_05_v3	chado	mRNA	301508	305191	.	-	.	ID=PF3D7_0507300.1;comment=The ortholog of  PF3D7_0507300 has been characterised in P. berghei as PIMMS2 (Plasmodium invasion of mosquito midgut screen candidate 2). Disruption of P. berghei PIMMS2 reduces the number of oocysts and sporozoites in Anopheles stephensi mosquitoes (PMID:28559405). PF3D7_0507300 has also been characterised in P. falciparum and named SOPT (subtilisin-like ookinete protein important for transmission). SOPT is expressed in ookinetes at the parasite periphery. SOPT-deficient parasites develop normally through the asexual and sexual stages and produce equivalent numbers of ookinetes%2C however%2C they form fewer oocysts and sporozoites in mosquitoes. SOPT-deficient parasites are unable to activate the immuneresponsive midgut invasion marker SRPN6 (serpin 6) after mosquito uptake%2C suggesting they are involved in ookinete invasion of the mosquito midgut epithelium. Disruption of SOPT has no effect on asexual growth%2C gametocytogenesis and sporozoite infectivity (PMID:29873127).;literature=PMID:29873127,PMID:28559405;Parent=PF3D7_0507300;Dbxref=MPMP:PF3D7_0507300,RMgm:PF3D7_0507300,OPI:PFE0360c,UniProtKB:Q8I429;gPI_anchor_cleavage_site=%3Bquery 871-871%3BGPI_cleavage_site_score%3D2.4940002;Ontology_term=GO:0009986,GO:0071944,GO:0044409,GO:0020036;controlled_curation=term%3DKnockout phenotype: dispensable in asexual stages%3Bcv%3DCC_genedb_controlledcuration%3Bdb_xref%3DPMID:29873127%3Bdate%3D20180608%3Bevidence%3DInferred from Mutant Phenotype;eupathdb_uc=100146473;orthologous_to=,Povale:PocGH01_10034200 link%3DPocGH01_10034200.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pberghei:PBANKA_1106900 link%3DPBANKA_1106900.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pchabaudi:PCHAS_1106600 link%3DPCHAS_1106600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C PvivaxP01:PVP01_1026700 link%3DPVP01_1026700.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0506500 link%3DPRCDC_0506500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pyoelii:PY17X_1108000 link%3DPY17X_110800