Pf3D7_05_v3	chado	pseudogenic_transcript	1329555	1330808	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_0533000.1;comment=Associated with GAGAGAA motif in 5'-untranslated region (PMID:17307259) A-type rifin (PMID:18197962) rif (repetitive interspersed family) genes were originally identified by Weber%3B they encode clonally variant RIFIN proteins%2C which are likely expressed on the infected erythrocyte surface%2C in Maurer's clefts and on merozoites. Originally classed with stevors%2C rifs are clearly a distinct family%2C with 150 or so copies per haploid genome. Surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion.;literature=PMID:2842673,PMID:10430943,PMID:17719658,PMID:10562315;Parent=PF3D7_0533000;Dbxref=MPMP:PF3D7_0533000;gPI_anchor_cleavage_site=%3Bquery 222-222%3BGPI_cleavage_site_score%3D0.16000001;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 315-335%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-343%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-291%3B;orthologous_to=Preichenowi:PRCDC_0531900 link%3DPRCDC_0531900.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Drifin%2C pseudogene%3B match_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL6069%3B rank%3D0,,PfalciparumIT:PFIT_0536700 link%3DPFIT_0536700.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Drifin%2C pseudogene%3B match_name%3Dorthomcl:orthomcl: PFIT_0536700.1:pep -> PF3D7_0533000.1:pep%3B rank%3D0;product=term%3Drifin%2C pseudogene%3B,rank%3D1%3Bterm%3DPIR protein%2C pseudogene%3B;signal_peptide=signalp%3B%3Bquery 1-21%3Bcleavage_site_probability%3D0.159;transmembrane_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 292-314%3B;translation=mqln+inislfslslnvlllsseiynqrnhyitlhtpstkptkpnrslceyelyaptnydndcemkkimenfdrvtrrrfeeynegiiknrqkckeqcdkdi#kiilkdkiekelteklstlqtdistndiptcvceksvadkvektfffgcggilctavpgwsiicsigfyaflntnameavvkadiakvlnelkeitvldtlfedklgslvtvetyacpnalnqaimvskesvcsvaglqrascgstrffipseivpkvhgatvegivvvkdaatktrntafsspfffflils#flq++#yv+llyfylfiylfiylilrysrkkkkmkkklqykkllke
