Pf3D7_06_v3	chado	mRNA	26557	27830	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_0600500.1;comment=A-type rifin (PMID:18197962) rif (repetitive interspersed family) genes were originally identified by Weber%3B they encode clonally variant RIFIN proteins%2C which are likely expressed on the infected erythrocyte surface%2C in Maurer's clefts and on merozoites. Originally classed with stevors%2C rifs are clearly a distinct family%2C with 150 or so copies per haploid genome. Surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion.;literature=PMID:2842673,PMID:10562315,PMID:17719658,PMID:10430943,PMID:25751816;Parent=PF3D7_0600500;Dbxref=UniProtKB:C6KSL1,MPMP:PF3D7_0600500;Ontology_term=GO:0020033,GO:0020002,GO:0020035,GO:0020013,GO:0020036,GO:0020003;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 353-372%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-373%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-329%3B;orthologous_to=Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0100400 link%3DPF3D7_0100400.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0937500 link%3DPF3D7_0937500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0833100 link%3DPF3D7_0833100.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B cluster_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL5276%3B program%3DOrthoMCL%3B rank%3D0;polypeptide_domain=pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF02009.12%3B%3BE()%3D6.3E-120%3Bscore%3D400.7%3Bquery 22-372%3Bdescription%3DRifin_STEVOR,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006373 :%09Variant surface antigen Rifin%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BTIGR_TIGRFAMS:TIGR01477%3B%3Bscore%3D1.8E-138%3Bquery 1-372%3Bdescription%3DVariant surface antigen Rifin,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006373 :%09Variant surface antigen Rifin%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BPfam:PF02009%3B%3Bscore%3D1.8E-129%3Bquery 34-372%3Bdescription%3DVariant surface antigen Rifin;product=term%3Drifin%3Bdb_xref%3DPMID:25751816%3Bevidence%3DInferred from Direct Assay,rank%3D1%3Bterm%3DPIR protein%3B;signal_peptide=signalp%3B%3Bquery 1-24%3Bcleavage_site_probability%3D0.169;transmembrane_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 330-352%3B;
