Pf3D7_07_v3	chado	mRNA	30097	31269	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_0700200.1;comment=rif (repetitive interspersed family) genes were originally identified by Weber%3B they encode clonally variant RIFIN proteins%2C which are likely expressed on the infected erythrocyte surface%2C in Maurer's clefts and on merozoites. Originally classed with stevors%2C rifs are clearly a distinct family%2C with 150 or so copies per haploid genome. Surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion. A-type rifin (PMID:18197962);literature=PMID:10430943,PMID:2842673,PMID:17719658,PMID:10562315,PMID:25751816;Parent=PF3D7_0700200;Dbxref=UniProtKB:C0H509,MPMP:PF3D7_0700200;gPI_anchor_cleavage_site=%3Bquery 285-285%3BGPI_cleavage_site_score%3D0.15480001;Ontology_term=GO:0020002,GO:0020036,GO:0020003,GO:0020033,GO:0020035,GO:0020013;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 304-323%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-324%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-280%3B;orthologous_to=Preichenowi:PRCDC_0040900 link%3DPRCDC_0040900.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1100400 link%3DPF3D7_1100400.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B cluster_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL5416%3B program%3DOrthoMCL%3B rank%3D0;polypeptide_domain=pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF02009.12%3B%3BE()%3D2.0E-113%3Bscore%3D379.3%3Bquery 20-323%3Bdescription%3DRifin_STEVOR,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006373 :%09Variant surface antigen Rifin%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BPfam:PF02009%3B%3Bscore%3D1.0E-17%3Bquery 261-323%3Bdescription%3DVariant surface antigen Rifin,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006373 :%09Variant surface antigen Rifin%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BPfam:PF02009%3B%3Bscore%3D2.3E-87%3Bquery 38-249%3Bdescription%3DVariant surface antigen Rifin,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006373 :%09Variant surface antigen Rifin%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BTIGR_TIGRFAMS:TIGR01477%3B%3Bscore%3D1.4E-121%3Bquery 1-323%3Bdescription%3DVariant surface antigen Rifin;product=term%3Drifin%3Bdb_xref%3DPMID:25751816%3Bevidence%3DInferred from Direct Assay,rank%3D1%3Bter