Pf3D7_07_v3	chado	pseudogenic_transcript	525063	526320	.	-	.	ID=PF3D7_0711900.1;comment=rif (repetitive interspersed family) genes were originally identified by Weber%3B they encode clonally variant RIFIN proteins%2C which are likely expressed on the infected erythrocyte surface%2C in Maurer's clefts and on merozoites. Originally classed with stevors%2C rifs are clearly a distinct family%2C with 150 or so copies per haploid genome. Surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion. A-type rifin (PMID:18197962);literature=PMID:10430943,PMID:2842673,PMID:10562315,PMID:17719658;Parent=PF3D7_0711900;Dbxref=OPI:MAL7P1.43,MPMP:PF3D7_0711900;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-4%3B,%3Bquery 337-355%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-358%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 28-313%3B;orthologous_to=PfalciparumIT:PFIT_1240800 link%3DPFIT_1240800.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Drifin%2C pseudogene%3B match_name%3Dorthomcl:orthomcl: PFIT_1240800.1:pep -> PF3D7_0711900.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0412600 link%3DPF3D7_0412600.1:1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0036800 link%3DPRCDC_0036800.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1240700 link%3DPF3D7_1240700.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_1239800 link%3DPRCDC_1239800.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0712200 link%3DPF3D7_0712200.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0043000 link%3DPRCDC_0043000.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B cluster_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL4928%3B program%3DOrthoMCL%3B rank%3D0;product=term%3Drifin%2C pseudogene%3B,rank%3D1%3Bterm%3DPIR protein%2C pseudogene%3B;transmembrane_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 5-27%3B,%3Bquery 314-336%3B;translation=mkiyyynillfylplnilltlyhqiiiylynylhiiwfidkcpngslhrytsynng#inknhidhyenvnythhlimimakkrnlccnnliiahnndyenmkkeckdqchkeiqkivlkdkiekelteklaalyrdiftediptcicekslsgkvektclkcggilgggleptvgllvtvavnqltktatvasiefatqegikagikavvhnlinvlhffdvtrdiwltlinsknyntvtglatsaktakeavgttcl