Pf3D7_07_v3	chado	mRNA	1357251	1363653	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_0731500.1;comment=EBA-175 is a merozoite micronemal protein involved in erythrocyte invasion via recognition of erythrocyte surface glycophorin A (PMID:1310320). EBA-175 binding to glycophorin A causes substantial changes in deformability of erythrocytes and activates a phosphorylation cascade that alters the viscoelastic properties of the host membrane (PMID:28226242). EBA175 binding to glycophorin A leads to an increase in the cytoskeletal tension of the red cell and a reduction in the bending modulus of the cell's membrane (PMID:28373555). EBA-175 mediates red blood cell clustering. This provides daughter merozoites ready access to uninfected red blood cells enhancing parasite growth (PMID:30556808).;literature=PMID:23268338,PMID:24043627,PMID:30556808,PMID:25205096,PMID:3901257,PMID:28226242,PMID:8009226,PMID:16051144,PMID:23717209,PMID:23457550,PMID:28373555;Parent=PF3D7_0731500;Dbxref=PDB:1ZRL,PDB:1ZRO,PDB:2RJI,MPMP:PF3D7_0731500,UniProtKB:Q8IBE8;Ontology_term=GO:0008201,GO:0075109,GO:0030260,GO:0046789,GO:0046789,GO:0020009,GO:0020009,GO:1903561,GO:0009405,GO:0016021;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1442-1502%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-1503%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-1418%3B;orthologous_to=Preichenowi:PRCDC_0728300 link%3DPRCDC_0728300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Derythrocyte binding antigen-175%3B match_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL6050%3B rank%3D0,Pknowlesi:PKNH_1400800 link%3DPKNH_1400800.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Derythrocyte binding protein (beta)%3Bmatch_name%3DPKNH_1400800.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,;polypeptide_domain=pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF05424.7%3B%3BE()%3D4.2E-18%3Bscore%3D65.9%3Bquery 179-321%3Bdescription%3DDuffy_binding,pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF05424.7%3B%3BE()%3D1.8E-16%3Bscore%3D60.6%3Bquery 487-614%3Bdescription%3DDuffy_binding,pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF11556.4%3B%3BE()%3D1.1E-31%3Bscore%3D108.9%3Bquery 1336-1415%3Bdescription%3DEBA-175_VI,iprscan%3B