Pf3D7_08_v3	chado	mRNA	1432696	1433932	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_0833400.1;comment=rif (repetitive interspersed family) genes were originally identified by Weber%3B they encode clonally variant RIFIN proteins%2C which are likely expressed on the infected erythrocyte surface%2C in Maurer's clefts and on merozoites. Originally classed with stevors%2C rifs are clearly a distinct family%2C with 150 or so copies per haploid genome. Surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion. A-type rifin (PMID:18197962);literature=PMID:10430943,PMID:25751816,PMID:2842673,PMID:17719658,PMID:10562315;Parent=PF3D7_0833400;Dbxref=UniProtKB:C0H4I2,MPMP:PF3D7_0833400;Ontology_term=GO:0020002,GO:0020036,GO:0020003,GO:0020033,GO:0020035,GO:0020013;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 321-340%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-341%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-297%3B;orthologous_to=Preichenowi:PRCDC_0033300 link%3DPRCDC_0033300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0031800 link%3DPRCDC_0031800.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0048200 link%3DPRCDC_0048200.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0040500 link%3DPRCDC_0040500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0007800 link%3DPRCDC_0007800.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B cluster_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL5016%3B program%3DOrthoMCL%3B rank%3D0,PfalciparumIT:PFIT_0537500 link%3DPFIT_0537500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Drifin%3B match_name%3Dorthomcl:orthomcl: PFIT_0537500.1:pep -> PF3D7_0833400.1:pep%3B rank%3D0;polypeptide_domain=pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF02009.12%3B%3BE()%3D5.0E-119%3Bscore%3D397.7%3Bquery 21-340%3Bdescription%3DRifin_STEVOR,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006373 :%09Variant surface antigen Rifin%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BTIGR_TIGRFAMS:TIGR01477%3B%3Bscore%3D1.4E-134%3Bquery 1-340%3Bdescription%3DVariant surface antigen Rifin,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006373 :%09Variant surface antigen Rifin%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BPfam:PF02009%3B%3Bscore%3D2.1E-122%3Bquery