Pf3D7_09_v3	chado	mRNA	55074	56081	.	-	.	ID=PF3D7_0900900.1;comment=stevor (subtelomeric%2C variable open reading frames) genes were originally identified as multicopy markers for fingerprinting parasites. With approximately 30 copies per haploid genome%2C they encode the STEVOR proteins%2C which are clonally variant%2C expressed on both merozoites and at the surface of infected erythrocytes. STEVOR is expressed much more prevalently in patient isolates than in laboratory isolates. Similar to (but clearly distinct from) RIFINs%2C surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion.;literature=PMID:14747138,PMID:19229319,PMID:25011110,PMID:18474651,PMID:1706114;Parent=PF3D7_0900900;Dbxref=MPMP:PF3D7_0900900,OPI:PFI0045c,UniProtKB:Q8I3D8;Ontology_term=GO:0020036,GO:0020013;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-181%3B,%3Bquery 284-300%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-301%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 205-260%3B;orthologous_to=Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0222800 link%3DPF3D7_0222800.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0222800.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0115400 link%3DPF3D7_0115400.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0115400.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0201300 link%3DPF3D7_0201300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0201300.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1040200 link%3DPF3D7_1040200.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1040200.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1254100 link%3DPF3D7_1254100.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1254100.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0901600 link%3DPF3D7_0901600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0901600.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0732000 link%3DPF3D7_0732000.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0732000.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0400800 link%3DPF3D7