Pf3D7_09_v3	chado	mRNA	1480947	1482211	.	-	.	ID=PF3D7_0937500.1;comment=A-type rifin (PMID:18197962) rif (repetitive interspersed family) genes were originally identified by Weber%3B they encode clonally variant RIFIN proteins%2C which are likely expressed on the infected erythrocyte surface%2C in Maurer's clefts and on merozoites. Originally classed with stevors%2C rifs are clearly a distinct family%2C with 150 or so copies per haploid genome. Surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion.;literature=PMID:10562315,PMID:2842673,PMID:17719658,PMID:25751816,PMID:10430943;Parent=PF3D7_0937500;Dbxref=MPMP:PF3D7_0937500,OPI:PFI1815c,UniProtKB:Q8I2E5;Ontology_term=GO:0020033,GO:0020002,GO:0020036,GO:0020003,GO:0020035,GO:0020013;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 350-369%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-370%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-326%3B;orthologous_to=Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0833100 link%3DPF3D7_0833100.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0600500 link%3DPF3D7_0600500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0100400 link%3DPF3D7_0100400.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B cluster_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL5276%3B program%3DOrthoMCL%3B rank%3D0;polypeptide_domain=pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF02009.12%3B%3BE()%3D1.9E-121%3Bscore%3D405.6%3Bquery 22-369%3Bdescription%3DRifin_STEVOR,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006373 :%09Variant surface antigen Rifin%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BTIGR_TIGRFAMS:TIGR01477%3B%3Bscore%3D3.1E-143%3Bquery 1-369%3Bdescription%3DVariant surface antigen Rifin,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006373 :%09Variant surface antigen Rifin%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BPfam:PF02009%3B%3Bscore%3D1.5E-132%3Bquery 31-369%3Bdescription%3DVariant surface antigen Rifin,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR011992 :%09EF-hand domain pair%3BSuperfamily:SSF47473%3B%3Bscore%3D9.11E-9%3Bquery 53-127%3Bdescription%3DEF-hand domain pair;product=term%3Drifin%3Bdb_xref%3DPMID:25751816%3Bevidence%3DInferred from Direct Assay,rank%3D1%3Bterm%3DPIR protein%3B;tran