Pf3D7_10_v3	chado	pseudogenic_transcript	57968	58980	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_1000800.1;comment=stevor (subtelomeric%2C variable open reading frames) genes were originally identified as multicopy markers for fingerprinting parasites. With approximately 30 copies per haploid genome%2C they encode the STEVOR proteins%2C which are clonally variant%2C expressed on both merozoites and at the surface of infected erythrocytes. STEVOR is expressed much more prevalently in patient isolates than in laboratory isolates. Similar to (but clearly distinct from) RIFINs%2C surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion.;literature=PMID:14747138,PMID:1706114,PMID:19229319,PMID:18474651;Parent=PF3D7_1000800;Dbxref=OPI:PF10_0009,MPMP:PF3D7_1000800;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 208-213%3B,%3Bquery 279-291%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-293%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-184%3B,%3Bquery 237-255%3B;orthologous_to=Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0425500 link%3DPF3D7_0425500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0500600 link%3DPF3D7_0500600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1372500 link%3DPF3D7_1372500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0221400 link%3DPF3D7_0221400.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0832000 link%3DPF3D7_0832000.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0402600 link%3DPF3D7_0402600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B cluster_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL4930%3B program%3DOrthoMCL%3B rank%3D0,PfalciparumIT:PFIT_1000100 link%3DPFIT_1000100.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Dstevor%3B match_name%3Dorthomcl:orthomcl: PFIT_1000100.1:pep -> PF3D7_1000800.1:pep%3B rank%3D0;product=term%3Dstevor%2C pseudogene%3B,rank%3D1%3Bterm%3DPIR protein%2C pseudogene%3B;signal_peptide=signalp%3B%3Bquery 1-20%3Bcleavage_site_probability%3D0.675;transmembrane_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 185-207%3B,%3Bquery 214-236%3B,%3Bquery 256-278%3B;translation=mllfallfnalllsqnvncrnnnynirftqtitqqtstksrhlaeierpknph#hndpelke