Pf3D7_10_v3	chado	pseudogenic_transcript	60024	61365	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_1000900.1;comment=var genes encode a family of clonally variant antigens collectively termed P. falciparum erythrocyte membrane protein 1 (PfEMP1). Mutually exclusive var gene regulation results in expression of a single PfEMP1 variant on the surface of each parasite-infected erythrocyte. Such expression coordination is critical in PfEMP1's role in evasion of host immune responses%2C but PfEMP1 is also involved in cytoadherence to host tissues and cells. Cytoadherence is associated with pathogenesis%2C implicating members of the PfEMP1 family as major virulence factors PfEMP1%2C truncated pseudogene%2C adjacent gene is also a PfEMP1 fragment%2C PF10_0011.;literature=PMID:7606788,PMID:7606775,PMID:6374009,PMID:11544371,PMID:7541722,PMID:18785843;Parent=PF3D7_1000900;Dbxref=OPI:PF10_0012,MPMP:PF3D7_1000900;orthologous_to=Preichenowi:PRCDC_1000300 link%3DPRCDC_1000300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Derythrocyte membrane protein 1 (EMP1)%2C pseudogene%3B match_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL6009%3B rank%3D0;product=term%3Derythrocyte membrane protein 1 (PfEMP1)%2C pseudogene%3B;translation=kpkitptrsnifrvndipqkdyslshksstiryipyrsgrykkniylhlrakngrlklywcyifieseyeefdindiypykspkyktlievvlkpseiygmkdthidhi+disdtttnkptdnewnqlkqdftaqylnhtgpyvplnnelpddniyt#pntlyfdnhdkkpfitsiqdifldsigeeatfnihwnvpeninrttnimnnpkyvsnniytgidlihdslsrnynvdihnemlkrkenelf*inhtknttfnrvskqthtipiknqlnlfhkwlgrnrdmcekgnhkedmlnkfndewttehkenmldipestlddihkindktynmisrnniyshndndkipldnlgstnisynyittnnnslqtnnlranisidihfdennnnventnvtgddhfenlynfcyiennnhekyevndntliyneynymnpkrivfr
