Pf3D7_10_v3	chado	mRNA	80302	82576	.	-	.	ID=PF3D7_1001500.1;comment=Early transcribed membrane protein (ETRAMP) family member.  Plasmodium conserved family with greater than ten members in P. falciparum.  ETRAMPs are abundantly expressed early in the intraerythrocytic cycle and are small (frequently less than 200 aa) integral membrane proteins that are localized within the parasitophorous vacuolar membrane (PVM).  All members have signal peptides plus a transmembrane domain.  Some members are expressed during hepatocyte development and their targeted gene disruption results in a block in hepatocyte development.;literature=PMID:12615320,PMID:15580261,PMID:12686607,PMID:15699336,PMID:16420351;Parent=PF3D7_1001500;Dbxref=OPI:PF10_0019,MPMP:PF3D7_1001500,UniProtKB:Q8IK21;Ontology_term=GO:0020005;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-6%3B,%3Bquery 70-107%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-108%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 28-46%3B;orthologous_to=Preichenowi:PRCDC_1000900 link%3DPRCDC_1000900.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Dearly transcribed membrane protein 10.1%3B match_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL6004%3B rank%3D0,PfalciparumIT:PFIT_1001100 link%3DPFIT_1001100.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Dearly transcribed membrane protein 10.1%3B match_name%3Dorthomcl:orthomcl: PFIT_1001100.1:pep -> PF3D7_1001500.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,;paralogous_to=Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1102700 link%3DPF3D7_1102700.1:pep type%3Dparalogous_to%3B match_name%3DORTHO_PARA_PF10_0019:pep_PF11_0039:pep%3B rank%3D2,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1016900 link%3DPF3D7_1016900.1:pep type%3Dparalogous_to%3B match_name%3DORTHO_PARA_PF10_0019:pep_PF10_0164:pep%3B rank%3D0;polypeptide_domain=pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF09716.6%3B%3BE()%3D3.2E-11%3Bscore%3D43.0%3Bquery 1-75%3Bdescription%3DETRAMP,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006389 :%09Early transcribed membrane protein (ETRAMP)%3BPfam:PF09716%3B%3Bscore%3D3.7E-11%3Bquery 1-74%3Bdescription%3DEarly transcribed membrane protein (ETRAMP),iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR