Pf3D7_10_v3	chado	mRNA	680750	683255	.	-	.	ID=PF3D7_1016900.1;comment=Early transcribed membrane protein (ETRAMP) family member.  Plasmodium conserved family with greater than ten members in P. falciparum.  ETRAMPs are abundantly expressed early in the intraerythrocytic cycle and are small (frequently less than 200 aa) integral membrane proteins that are localized within the parasitophorous vacuolar membrane (PVM).  All members have signal peptides plus a transmembrane domain.  Some members are expressed during hepatocyte development and their targeted gene disruption results in a block in hepatocyte development. Gene prediction formerly had a second small exon. Characterisation of the ETRAMP gene family showed that this exon was incorrect (PMID:12686607);literature=PMID:16420351,PMID:20228203,PMID:12686607,PMID:15699336;Parent=PF3D7_1016900;Dbxref=MPMP:PF3D7_1016900,RMgm:PF3D7_1016900,UniProtKB:Q8IJM9;gPI_anchor_cleavage_site=%3Bquery 90-90%3BGPI_cleavage_site_score%3D0.52;Ontology_term=GO:0020005;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-6%3B,%3Bquery 76-108%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-109%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 30-52%3B;orthologous_to=,PfalciparumIT:PFIT_1016400 link%3DPFIT_1016400.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Dearly transcribed membrane protein 10.3%3B match_name%3Dorthomcl:orthomcl: PFIT_1016400.1:pep -> PF3D7_1016900.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Preichenowi:PRCDC_1016300 link%3DPRCDC_1016300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Dearly transcribed membrane protein 10.3%3B match_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL5994%3B rank%3D0;paralogous_to=Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1001500 link%3DPF3D7_1001500.1:pep type%3Dparalogous_to%3B match_name%3DORTHO_PARA_PF10_0019:pep_PF10_0164:pep%3B rank%3D0;polypeptide_domain=pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF09716.6%3B%3BE()%3D4.6E-17%3Bscore%3D61.7%3Bquery 1-81%3Bdescription%3DETRAMP,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006389 :%09Early transcribed membrane protein (ETRAMP)%3BPfam:PF09716%3B%3Bscore%3D4.1E-17%3Bquery 1-81%3Bdescriptio