Pf3D7_10_v3	chado	mRNA	1333997	1336551	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_1033200.1;comment=Early transcribed membrane protein (ETRAMP) family member.  Plasmodium conserved family with greater than ten members in P. falciparum.  ETRAMPs are abundantly expressed early in the intraerythrocytic cycle and are small (frequently less than 200 aa) integral membrane proteins that are localized within the parasitophorous vacuolar membrane (PVM).  All members have signal peptides plus a transmembrane domain.  Some members are expressed during hepatocyte development and their targeted gene disruption results in a block in hepatocyte development.;literature=PMID:15671043,PMID:16420351,PMID:12615320,PMID:15580261,PMID:12686607,PMID:15699336;Parent=PF3D7_1033200;Dbxref=OPI:PF10_0323,MPMP:PF3D7_1033200,RMgm:PF3D7_1033200,UniProtKB:Q8IJ76;gPI_anchor_cleavage_site=%3Bquery 339-339%3BGPI_cleavage_site_score%3D2.1199;Ontology_term=GO:0020036,GO:0020005,GO:0005634;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 24-52%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-356%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-5%3B,%3Bquery 76-355%3B;orthologous_to=,Pberghei:PBANKA_0517000 link%3DPBANKA_0517000.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Dearly transcribed membrane protein%3B match_name%3DORTHO_PARA_PF3D7_1033200.1:pep_PBANKA_0517000.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Preichenowi:PRCDC_1032500 link%3DPRCDC_1032500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pknowlesi:PKNH_0618000 link%3DPKNH_0618000.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C PvivaxP01:PVP01_0618300 link%3DPVP01_0618300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B cluster_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL5251%3B program%3DOrthoMCL%3B rank%3D0;polypeptide_domain=pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF09716.6%3B%3BE()%3D4.1E-15%3Bscore%3D55.5%3Bquery 1-81%3Bdescription%3DETRAMP,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006389 :%09Early transcribed membrane protein (ETRAMP)%3BTIGR_TIGRFAMS:TIGR01495%3B%3Bscore%3D1.1E-28%3Bquery 1-88%3Bdescription%3DEarly transcribed membrane protein (ETRAMP),iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006389 :%09Early transcribed membrane prote