Pf3D7_10_v3	chado	mRNA	1605876	1607228	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_1040200.1;comment=stevor (subtelomeric%2C variable open reading frames) genes were originally identified as multicopy markers for fingerprinting parasites. With approximately 30 copies per haploid genome%2C they encode the STEVOR proteins%2C which are clonally variant%2C expressed on both merozoites and at the surface of infected erythrocytes. STEVOR is expressed much more prevalently in patient isolates than in laboratory isolates. Similar to (but clearly distinct from) RIFINs%2C surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion.;literature=PMID:1706114,PMID:31363031,PMID:25011110,PMID:19229319,PMID:18474651,PMID:14747138;Parent=PF3D7_1040200;Dbxref=OPI:PF10_0395,MPMP:PF3D7_1040200,UniProtKB:Q8IJ07;Ontology_term=GO:0020013,GO:0033644;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-182%3B,%3Bquery 289-305%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-306%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 206-265%3B;orthologous_to=Preichenowi:PRCDC_0053800 link%3DPRCDC_0053800.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0201300 link%3DPF3D7_0201300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1479900 link%3DPF3D7_1479900.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0115400 link%3DPF3D7_0115400.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0200400 link%3DPF3D7_0200400.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0049000 link%3DPRCDC_0049000.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0301600 link%3DPRCDC_0301600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B cluster_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL4881%3B program%3DOrthoMCL%3B rank%3D0;polypeptide_domain=pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF02009.12%3B%3BE()%3D9.0E-15%3Bscore%3D55.2%3Bquery 243-305%3Bdescription%3DRifin_STEVOR,pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF02009.12%3B%3BE()%3D1.9E-32%3Bscore%3D113.3%3Bquery 26-214%3Bdescription%3DRifin_STEVOR,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006374 :%09Variant surface antigen Stevor%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BTIGR_TIGRFAMS:TIGR01478%3B%3Bscore%3D9.0E-137%3Bquery 1-305%3Bd