Pf3D7_10_v3	chado	mRNA	1628914	1630023	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_1040900.1;comment=rif (repetitive interspersed family) genes were originally identified by Weber%3B they encode clonally variant RIFIN proteins%2C which are likely expressed on the infected erythrocyte surface%2C in Maurer's clefts and on merozoites. Originally classed with stevors%2C rifs are clearly a distinct family%2C with 150 or so copies per haploid genome. Surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion. B-type rifin (PMID:18197962);literature=PMID:2842673,PMID:10562315,PMID:17719658,PMID:10430943;Parent=PF3D7_1040900;Dbxref=MPMP:PF3D7_1040900,UniProtKB:Q8IJ00;Ontology_term=GO:0020002,GO:0016020,GO:0020033;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 292-311%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-312%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-268%3B;orthologous_to=Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1040800 link%3DPF3D7_1040800.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Drifin%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1040800.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1480000 link%3DPF3D7_1480000.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3DPIR protein%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1480000.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1040100 link%3DPF3D7_1040100.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Drifin%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1040100.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0300500 link%3DPF3D7_0300500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Drifin%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0300500.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1040700 link%3DPF3D7_1040700.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Drifin%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1040700.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0200500 link%3DPF3D7_0200500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Drifin%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0200500.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0400500 link%3DPF3D7_0400500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Drifin%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0400500.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1300600 link%3DPF3D7_1300600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3DPIR protein%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1300600.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D