Pf3D7_11_v3	chado	pseudogenic_transcript	56792	57840	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_1100700.1;comment=stevor (subtelomeric%2C variable open reading frames) genes were originally identified as multicopy markers for fingerprinting parasites. With approximately 30 copies per haploid genome%2C they encode the STEVOR proteins%2C which are clonally variant%2C expressed on both merozoites and at the surface of infected erythrocytes. STEVOR is expressed much more prevalently in patient isolates than in laboratory isolates. Similar to (but clearly distinct from) RIFINs%2C surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion.;literature=PMID:19229319,PMID:14747138,PMID:1706114,PMID:18474651;Parent=PF3D7_1100700;Dbxref=MPMP:PF3D7_1100700;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 27-192%3B,%3Bquery 269-286%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-288%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-3%3B,%3Bquery 216-245%3B;orthologous_to=Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0700700 link%3DPF3D7_0700700.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0832600 link%3DPF3D7_0832600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B cluster_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL5415%3B program%3DOrthoMCL%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1040200 link%3DPF3D7_1040200.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1040200.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1479500 link%3DPF3D7_1479500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1479500.1:pep%3B rank%3D0;product=term%3Dstevor%2C pseudogene%3B,rank%3D1%3Bterm%3DPIR protein%2C pseudogene%3B;transmembrane_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 4-26%3B,%3Bquery 193-215%3B,%3Bquery 246-268%3B;translation=misynlkliifsiilvtlsliynndyerlyknmkyknfvlvpinfrslaev#ferttnhiyrndklreytstnekkyhknnylkddakteqnitdvtekeitertkskkyrkgtydaekkeksnissrflrylemqrklynnfyvkteidfenfsnksnnkscecinknksyhiltssnkvhdkyldnlkercvggvgictflseatvysgvvagaailekvsntpvglwlptetykvsfltsnflpygiaiavfiaviiiviflyvylrnrrkhswkyeckkhlcr
