Pf3D7_11_v3	chado	pseudogenic_transcript	64441	64842	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_1101000.1;comment=var genes encode a family of clonally variant antigens collectively termed P. falciparum erythrocyte membrane protein 1 (PfEMP1). Mutually exclusive var gene regulation results in expression of a single PfEMP1 variant on the surface of each parasite-infected erythrocyte. Such expression coordination is critical in PfEMP1's role in evasion of host immune responses%2C but PfEMP1 is also involved in cytoadherence to host tissues and cells. Cytoadherence is associated with pathogenesis%2C implicating members of the PfEMP1 family as major virulence factors;literature=PMID:6374009,PMID:7541722,PMID:11544371,PMID:7606775,PMID:18785843,PMID:7606788;Parent=PF3D7_1101000;Dbxref=OPI:PF11_0522,MPMP:PF3D7_1101000;polypeptide_domain=pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF15445.2%3B%3BE()%3D4.1E-57%3Bscore%3D194.4%3Bquery 4-133%3Bdescription%3DATS,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR029211 :%09Plasmodium falciparum erythrocyte membrane protein 1%2C acidic terminal segment%3BPfam:PF15445%3B%3Bscore%3D4.2E-57%3Bquery 4-133%3Bdescription%3DPlasmodium falciparum erythrocyte membrane protein 1%2C acidic terminal segment;product=term%3Derythrocyte membrane protein 1 (PfEMP1)%2C pseudogene%3B;translation=mdrrhrdmceklkndnerlaklkeewenethsgnthpsesnktlntdvsiqihmdnpkpinqfnnmdtiledldkynepyydvqddiyydvndhdtstvdsnnmdvpskvqiemdvntklvkekypiadvwdi
