Pf3D7_11_v3	chado	mRNA	127762	130186	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_1102700.1;comment=Early transcribed membrane protein (ETRAMP) family member.  Plasmodium conserved family with greater than ten members in P. falciparum.  ETRAMPs are abundantly expressed early in the intraerythrocytic cycle and are small (frequently less than 200 aa) integral membrane proteins that are localized within the parasitophorous vacuolar membrane (PVM).  All members have signal peptides plus a transmembrane domain.  Some members are expressed during hepatocyte development and their targeted gene disruption results in a block in hepatocyte development. This version has an adjacent paralogous gene%2C PF11_0040.;literature=PMID:15699336,PMID:12615320,PMID:16420351,PMID:12686607,PMID:15580261;Parent=PF3D7_1102700;Dbxref=OPI:PF11_0039,MPMP:PF3D7_1102700,UniProtKB:Q7KQK8;gPI_anchor_cleavage_site=%3Bquery 62-62%3BGPI_cleavage_site_score%3D0.43200004;Ontology_term=GO:0020005;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-6%3B,%3Bquery 72-91%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-92%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 30-48%3B;orthologous_to=,Preichenowi:PRCDC_1101200 link%3DPRCDC_1101200.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Dearly transcribed membrane protein 11.1%3B match_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL5967%3B rank%3D0,PfalciparumIT:PFIT_1103500 link%3DPFIT_1103500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Dearly transcribed membrane protein 11.1%3B match_name%3Dorthomcl:orthomcl: PFIT_1103500.1:pep -> PF3D7_1102700.1:pep%3B rank%3D0;paralogous_to=Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1102800 link%3DPF3D7_1102800.1:pep type%3Dparalogous_to%3B match_name%3DORTHO_PARA_PF11_0039:pep_PF11_0040:pep%3B rank%3D1,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1001500 link%3DPF3D7_1001500.1:pep type%3Dparalogous_to%3B match_name%3DORTHO_PARA_PF10_0019:pep_PF11_0039:pep%3B rank%3D0;polypeptide_domain=pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF09716.6%3B%3BE()%3D7.5E-13%3Bscore%3D48.2%3Bquery 1-75%3Bdescription%3DETRAMP,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006389 :%09Early transcribed membrane protein (E