Pf3D7_11_v3	chado	mRNA	2009875	2010902	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_1149900.1;comment=Associated with GAGAGAA motif in 5'-untranslated region (PMID:17307259) stevor (subtelomeric%2C variable open reading frames) genes were originally identified as multicopy markers for fingerprinting parasites. With approximately 30 copies per haploid genome%2C they encode the STEVOR proteins%2C which are clonally variant%2C expressed on both merozoites and at the surface of infected erythrocytes. STEVOR is expressed much more prevalently in patient isolates than in laboratory isolates. Similar to (but clearly distinct from) RIFINs%2C surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion.;literature=PMID:1706114,PMID:14747138,PMID:25011110,PMID:18474651,PMID:19229319;Parent=PF3D7_1149900;Dbxref=MPMP:PF3D7_1149900,UniProtKB:Q8IHM4;Ontology_term=GO:0016020,GO:0020036,GO:0020013;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 200-205%3B,%3Bquery 292-308%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-309%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-176%3B,%3Bquery 229-268%3B;orthologous_to=Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0732000 link%3DPF3D7_0732000.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0732000.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1040200 link%3DPF3D7_1040200.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1040200.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0617600 link%3DPF3D7_0617600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0617600.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0101800 link%3DPF3D7_0101800.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0101800.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0400800 link%3DPF3D7_0400800.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0400800.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0102100 link%3DPF3D7_0102100.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%2C pseudogene%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0102100.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1254300 link%3DPF3D7_1254300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous