Pf3D7_12_v3	chado	mRNA	1684977	1686307	.	-	.	ID=PF3D7_1240100.1;comment=Early transcribed membrane protein (ETRAMP) family member.  Plasmodium conserved family with greater than ten members in P. falciparum.  ETRAMPs are abundantly expressed early in the intraerythrocytic cycle and are small (frequently less than 200 aa) integral membrane proteins that are localized within the parasitophorous vacuolar membrane (PVM).  All members have signal peptides plus a transmembrane domain.  Some members are expressed during hepatocyte development and their targeted gene disruption results in a block in hepatocyte development. member of etramps family%2C some of which%2C but not yet this one%2C have been localized to parasitophorous vacuolar membrane (PVM) or to tubovesicular extensions of the PVM;literature=PMID:12686607,PMID:16420351,PMID:15699336,PMID:15580261,PMID:12615320;Parent=PF3D7_1240100;Dbxref=MPMP:PF3D7_1240100,OPI:PFL1945c,UniProtKB:Q8I522;Ontology_term=GO:0016020;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 26-53%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-106%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-5%3B,%3Bquery 77-105%3B;orthologous_to=,Preichenowi:PRCDC_1239300 link%3DPRCDC_1239300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Dearly transcribed membrane protein 12%3B match_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL5938%3B rank%3D0;polypeptide_domain=pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF09716.6%3B%3BE()%3D4.9E-21%3Bscore%3D74.5%3Bquery 1-81%3Bdescription%3DETRAMP,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006389 :%09Early transcribed membrane protein (ETRAMP)%3BPfam:PF09716%3B%3Bscore%3D5.3E-21%3Bquery 1-81%3Bdescription%3DEarly transcribed membrane protein (ETRAMP),iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006389 :%09Early transcribed membrane protein (ETRAMP)%3BTIGR_TIGRFAMS:TIGR01495%3B%3Bscore%3D3.0E-31%3Bquery 1-86%3Bdescription%3DEarly transcribed membrane protein (ETRAMP);product=term%3Dearly transcribed membrane protein 12%3B;signal_peptide=signalp%3B%3Bquery 1-26%3Bcleavage_site_probability%3D0.351;transmembrane_polypeptide_region