Pf3D7_12_v3	chado	mRNA	2228632	2229740	.	-	.	ID=PF3D7_1254800.1;comment=A-type rifin (PMID:18197962) rif (repetitive interspersed family) genes were originally identified by Weber%3B they encode clonally variant RIFIN proteins%2C which are likely expressed on the infected erythrocyte surface%2C in Maurer's clefts and on merozoites. Originally classed with stevors%2C rifs are clearly a distinct family%2C with 150 or so copies per haploid genome. Surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion. Binds to leucocyte immunoglobulin-like receptor B1 (LILRB1) and inhibits activation of LILRB1-expressing B cells and natural killer cells (PMID:29187532).;literature=PMID:10430943,PMID:17719658,PMID:10562315,PMID:29187532,PMID:25751816,PMID:2842673;Parent=PF3D7_1254800;Dbxref=MPMP:PF3D7_1254800,OPI:PFL2645c,UniProtKB:Q8I4N9;gPI_anchor_cleavage_site=%3Bquery 279-279%3BGPI_cleavage_site_score%3D0.15480001;Ontology_term=GO:0020033,GO:0020002,GO:0020036,GO:0020003,GO:0020035,GO:0020013,GO:0046789,GO:0020012;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 298-317%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-318%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-274%3B;polypeptide_domain=pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF02009.12%3B%3BE()%3D4.5E-110%3Bscore%3D368.3%3Bquery 22-317%3Bdescription%3DRifin_STEVOR,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006373 :%09Variant surface antigen Rifin%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BTIGR_TIGRFAMS:TIGR01477%3B%3Bscore%3D1.1E-119%3Bquery 1-317%3Bdescription%3DVariant surface antigen Rifin,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006373 :%09Variant surface antigen Rifin%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BPfam:PF02009%3B%3Bscore%3D2.7E-100%3Bquery 31-317%3Bdescription%3DVariant surface antigen Rifin;product=term%3Drifin%3Bdb_xref%3DPMID:25751816%3Bevidence%3DInferred from Direct Assay,rank%3D1%3Bterm%3DPIR protein%3B;transmembrane_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 275-297%3B;
