Pf3D7_13_v3	chado	mRNA	2863866	2864869	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_1372800.1;comment=stevor (subtelomeric%2C variable open reading frames) genes were originally identified as multicopy markers for fingerprinting parasites. With approximately 30 copies per haploid genome%2C they encode the STEVOR proteins%2C which are clonally variant%2C expressed on both merozoites and at the surface of infected erythrocytes. STEVOR is expressed much more prevalently in patient isolates than in laboratory isolates. Similar to (but clearly distinct from) RIFINs%2C surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion.;literature=PMID:25011110,PMID:19229319,PMID:18474651,PMID:14747138,PMID:1706114;Parent=PF3D7_1372800;Dbxref=UniProtKB:C0H5N4,OPI:MAL13P1.505,MPMP:PF3D7_1372800;Ontology_term=GO:0020036,GO:0020013;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-178%3B,%3Bquery 284-300%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-301%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 199-260%3B;orthologous_to=Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1254300 link%3DPF3D7_1254300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1254300.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0200400 link%3DPF3D7_0200400.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0200400.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0101800 link%3DPF3D7_0101800.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0101800.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0901600 link%3DPF3D7_0901600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0901600.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0402600 link%3DPF3D7_0402600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0402600.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1479500 link%3DPF3D7_1479500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1479500.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,PfalciparumIT:PFIT_0300300 link%3DPFIT_0300300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Dstevor%3B match_name%3Dorthomcl:orthomcl: PFIT_0300300.1:pep -> PF3D7_1372800.1:pep%