Pf3D7_14_v3	chado	mRNA	24337	25320	.	-	.	ID=PF3D7_1400700.1;comment=stevor (subtelomeric%2C variable open reading frames) genes were originally identified as multicopy markers for fingerprinting parasites. With approximately 30 copies per haploid genome%2C they encode the STEVOR proteins%2C which are clonally variant%2C expressed on both merozoites and at the surface of infected erythrocytes. STEVOR is expressed much more prevalently in patient isolates than in laboratory isolates. Similar to (but clearly distinct from) RIFINs%2C surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion.;literature=PMID:25011110,PMID:14747138,PMID:1706114,PMID:19229319,PMID:18474651;Parent=PF3D7_1400700;Dbxref=OPI:PF14_0007,MPMP:PF3D7_1400700,UniProtKB:Q8IM81;Ontology_term=GO:0016020,GO:0020036,GO:0020013;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-178%3B,%3Bquery 277-293%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-294%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 202-253%3B;orthologous_to=Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0631900 link%3DPF3D7_0631900.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0631900.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1100700 link%3DPF3D7_1100700.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%2C pseudogene%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1100700.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,PfalciparumIT:PFIT_0731100 link%3DPFIT_0731100.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Dstevor%3B match_name%3Dorthomcl:orthomcl: PFIT_0731100.1:pep -> PF3D7_1400700.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Preichenowi:PRCDC_0035200 link%3DPRCDC_0035200.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Dstevor%3B match_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL5895%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1149900 link%3DPF3D7_1149900.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1149900.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0732000 link%3DPF3D7_0732000.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0732000.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0300900 link%3DPF3D7_0300900.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_na