Pf3D7_14_v3	chado	mRNA	52256	54457	.	-	.	ID=PF3D7_1401400.1;comment=Early transcribed membrane protein (ETRAMP) family member.  Plasmodium conserved family with greater than ten members in P. falciparum.  ETRAMPs are abundantly expressed early in the intraerythrocytic cycle and are small (frequently less than 200 aa) integral membrane proteins that are localized within the parasitophorous vacuolar membrane (PVM).  All members have signal peptides plus a transmembrane domain.  Some members are expressed during hepatocyte development and their targeted gene disruption results in a block in hepatocyte development.;literature=PMID:15699336,PMID:16420351,PMID:12686607,PMID:12615320,PMID:15580261;Parent=PF3D7_1401400;Dbxref=OPI:PF14_0016,MPMP:PF3D7_1401400,UniProtKB:Q7KQM5;gPI_anchor_cleavage_site=%3Bquery 89-89%3BGPI_cleavage_site_score%3D0.78000003;Ontology_term=GO:0020005;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-4%3B,%3Bquery 75-107%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-108%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 28-51%3B;orthologous_to=Preichenowi:PRCDC_1400700 link%3DPRCDC_1400700.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Dearly transcribed membrane protein 14.1%3B match_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL5891%3B rank%3D0,PfalciparumIT:PFIT_1402300 link%3DPFIT_1402300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B product%3Dearly transcribed membrane protein 14.1%3B match_name%3Dorthomcl:orthomcl: PFIT_1402300.1:pep -> PF3D7_1401400.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1001500 link%3DPF3D7_1001500.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dearly transcribed membrane protein 10.1%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_1001500.1:pep%3B rank%3D0;polypeptide_domain=pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF09716.6%3B%3BE()%3D4.2E-20%3Bscore%3D71.5%3Bquery 1-80%3Bdescription%3DETRAMP,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006389 :%09Early transcribed membrane protein (ETRAMP)%3BTIGR_TIGRFAMS:TIGR01495%3B%3Bscore%3D1.0E-33%3Bquery 1-85%3Bdescription%3DEarly transcribed membrane protein (ETRAMP),iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006389 :%09Early transcribed mem