Pf3D7_14_v3	chado	mRNA	2903947	2907414	.	-	.	ID=PF3D7_1471100.1;comment=EXP2 is a component of the PTEX complex (Plasmodium translocon of exported proteins) (PMID:19536257). EXP2 serves dual roles as a protein-conducting channel (PMID:30150771%2C PMID:30150733) and as a channel able to facilitate nutrient passage across the parasitophorous vacuole membrane (PVM) (PMID:30150733). Knockdown of EXP2 reduces growth and protein export (PMID:30439948). The N-terminus of EXP2 forms the membrane-associated pore of the protein exporting translocon PTEX (PMID:30476118).;literature=PMID:26347246,PMID:30476118,PMID:30439948,PMID:30150771,PMID:22253438,PMID:30150733,PMID:9574909,PMID:19536257,PMID:25662767,PMID:27168322;Parent=PF3D7_1471100;Dbxref=OPI:PF14_0678,MPMP:PF3D7_1471100,RMgm:PF3D7_1471100,UniProtKB:Q8IKC8;gPI_anchor_cleavage_site=%3Bquery 271-271%3BGPI_cleavage_site_score%3D0.46799996;Ontology_term=GO:0020005,GO:0005515,GO:0005515,GO:0044161,GO:0097619,GO:0005515,GO:0005515,GO:0020026,GO:0015267,GO:0097619,GO:0044658,GO:0005634,GO:1903561,GO:0005515;controlled_curation=term%3Dconditional knockdown: essential%3Bcv%3DCC_genedb_controlledcuration%3Bdb_xref%3DPMID:30150733%3Bdate%3D20180830%3Bevidence%3DInferred from Mutant Phenotype;orthologous_to=Pberghei:PBANKA_1334300 link%3DPBANKA_1334300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_1470300 link%3DPRCDC_1470300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C PvivaxP01:PVP01_1235700 link%3DPVP01_1235700.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pyoelii:PY17X_1339000 link%3DPY17X_1339000.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pgallinaceum:PGAL8A_00230600 link%3DPGAL8A_00230600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Povale:PocGH01_12043700 link%3DPocGH01_12043700.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pchabaudi:PCHAS_1338900 link%3DPCHAS_1338900.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pknowlesi:PKNH_1209900 link%3DPKNH_1209900.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pmalariae:PmUG01_12045800 link%3DPmUG01_12045800.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Prelictum:PRELSG_1209600 link%3DPRELSG_12