Pf3D7_14_v3	chado	mRNA	3269494	3270496	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_1479500.1;comment=stevor (subtelomeric%2C variable open reading frames) genes were originally identified as multicopy markers for fingerprinting parasites. With approximately 30 copies per haploid genome%2C they encode the STEVOR proteins%2C which are clonally variant%2C expressed on both merozoites and at the surface of infected erythrocytes. STEVOR is expressed much more prevalently in patient isolates than in laboratory isolates. Similar to (but clearly distinct from) RIFINs%2C surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion.;literature=PMID:18474651,PMID:14747138,PMID:1706114,PMID:25011110,PMID:19229319;Parent=PF3D7_1479500;Dbxref=OPI:PF14_0767,MPMP:PF3D7_1479500,UniProtKB:Q8IK43;Ontology_term=GO:0020036,GO:0016020,GO:0020013;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-174%3B,%3Bquery 283-299%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-300%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 198-259%3B;orthologous_to=Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0300400 link%3DPF3D7_0300400.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_1254100 link%3DPF3D7_1254100.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0700400 link%3DPF3D7_0700400.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0732000 link%3DPF3D7_0732000.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Preichenowi:PRCDC_0009200 link%3DPRCDC_0009200.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%2C Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0900900 link%3DPF3D7_0900900.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3B cluster_name%3DPlasmodium:ORTHOMCL4929%3B program%3DOrthoMCL%3B rank%3D0;polypeptide_domain=pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF02009.12%3B%3BE()%3D2.3E-33%3Bscore%3D116.3%3Bquery 37-198%3Bdescription%3DRifin_STEVOR,pfam_scan%3BPfam:PF02009.12%3B%3BE()%3D9.6E-16%3Bscore%3D58.4%3Bquery 248-299%3Bdescription%3DRifin_STEVOR,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006374 :%09Variant surface antigen Stevor%2C Plasmodium falciparum%3BPfam:PF17410%3B%3Bscore%3D8.5E-139%3Bquery 31-299%3Bdescription%3DVariant surface antigen Stevor,iprscan%3BInterPro:IPR006374 :%09Variant surfac