Pf3D7_14_v3	chado	mRNA	3282729	3283752	.	+	.	ID=PF3D7_1479900.1;comment=stevor (subtelomeric%2C variable open reading frames) genes were originally identified as multicopy markers for fingerprinting parasites. With approximately 30 copies per haploid genome%2C they encode the STEVOR proteins%2C which are clonally variant%2C expressed on both merozoites and at the surface of infected erythrocytes. STEVOR is expressed much more prevalently in patient isolates than in laboratory isolates. Similar to (but clearly distinct from) RIFINs%2C surface expression indicates possible role in immune evasion.;literature=PMID:1706114,PMID:19229319,PMID:18474651,PMID:25011110,PMID:14747138;Parent=PF3D7_1479900;Dbxref=MPMP:PF3D7_1479900,UniProtKB:Q8IK39;Ontology_term=GO:0016020,GO:0020036,GO:0020013;cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 24-178%3B,%3Bquery 288-304%3B;membrane_structure=tmhmm%3B%3Bquery 1-305%3B;non_cytoplasmic_polypeptide_region=%3Bquery 1-3%3B,%3Bquery 202-264%3B;orthologous_to=Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0201300 link%3DPF3D7_0201300.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0201300.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0617600 link%3DPF3D7_0617600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0617600.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0324600 link%3DPF3D7_0324600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0324600.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0200900 link%3DPF3D7_0200900.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%2C pseudogene%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0200900.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0732000 link%3DPF3D7_0732000.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0732000.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0221400 link%3DPF3D7_0221400.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0221400.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalciparum:PF3D7_0901600 link%3DPF3D7_0901600.1:pep type%3Dorthologous_to%3Bproduct%3Dstevor%3Bmatch_name%3DPF3D7_0901600.1:pep%3B rank%3D0,Pfalc